      "title": "READ BEFORE RUNNING",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "TRUE H3 STILL: one sampled temporal latent frame. The native conditioning node still shows length=5; its LATENT output is intentionally unused. No audio decoder or frame extraction is used.\n\nIMPORTANT CURRENT-CORE UPDATE: the pinned native H3 VAE already repeats a T=1 latent into five copies and keeps pixel frame 3. Use native VAEDecode here. The old Fizgig Still Decode is redundant on this pin.\n\nThe current best-documented high-resolution example uses FL2VA, 50 steps, er_sde/simple, and no Turbo. This graph keeps full BF16 weights and the FP16 video VAE. These precision changes are not benchmark-proven improvements.\n\nReference stills use your existing Ref2VA checkpoint and one authoritative reference. 2.5 MP is the edit baseline; 8.4 MP is a higher-resolution adaptation, not a verified identity upgrade. Multiple-reference still edits have an unresolved report dated 2026-10-20. \n\nSource size preserves framing approximately after 32-pixel rounding. Up to 4096 per side is accepted by the node, not a demonstrated quality ceiling. No generative upscale is applied.\n\nThe reference is conditioning, not a pixel lock. Keep denoise=1: lowering denoise on an empty latent does not preserve the original photograph.\n\nAll new workflows are source-reviewed and offline-tested only. Docker/GPU inference and face fidelity still need live validation. No promise of exact identity."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "TRUE H3 STILL: one sampled temporal latent frame. The native conditioning node still shows length=5; its LATENT output is intentionally unused. No audio decoder or frame extraction is used.\n\nIMPORTANT CURRENT-CORE UPDATE: the pinned native H3 VAE already repeats a T=1 latent into five copies and keeps pixel frame 3. Use native VAEDecode here. The old Fizgig Still Decode is redundant on this pin.\n\nThe current best-documented high-resolution example uses FL2VA, 50 steps, er_sde/simple, and no Turbo. This graph keeps full BF16 weights and the FP16 video VAE. These precision changes are not benchmark-proven improvements.\n\nReference stills use your existing Ref2VA checkpoint and one authoritative reference. 2.5 MP is the edit baseline; 8.4 MP is a higher-resolution adaptation, not a verified identity upgrade. Multiple-reference still edits have an unresolved report dated 2026-10-20. \n\nSource size preserves framing approximately after 32-pixel rounding. Up to 4096 per side is accepted by the node, not a demonstrated quality ceiling. No generative upscale is applied.\n\nThe reference is conditioning, not a pixel lock. Keep denoise=1: lowering denoise on an empty latent does not preserve the original photograph.\n\nAll new workflows are source-reviewed and offline-tested only. Docker/GPU inference and face fidelity still need live validation. No promise of exact identity."
      }
    }
